From f31377fce6ec31114e5a4398c0e5270552bce09f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcos Benedicto <marsanben92@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 13:21:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make secure mode the default and keep interpreters out
 of the allowlist

Two default-path weaknesses let "secure mode" run unrestricted, reported via
GitHub private vulnerability reporting and security advisories:

- The bare binary shipped with Security.Enabled=false, so the documented
  from-source install ran an unrestricted shell (GHSA-f5pj-2738-996m #1).
- The default security.yaml allowlisted /bin/bash, /usr/bin/python3 and
  /usr/bin/git. Allowlisting an interpreter defeats the allowlist entirely
  (GHSA-3x77-wg38-92r3, GHSA-74hp-mggr-hv58).
- '!' was missing from the metacharacter blocklist, enabling the git
  shell-alias bypass `git -c alias.x=!cmd` (GHSA-74hp-mggr-hv58).

Changes:
- Embed secure defaults: the server now boots in secure mode restricted to a
  narrow allowlist of read-only utilities with no config file required.
  Unrestricted mode requires explicit MCP_SHELL_ALLOW_UNSAFE=true opt-in.
- Drop shell/language interpreters from the default security.yaml and warn at
  startup if an interpreter or alias-capable tool is allowlisted.
- Block '!' and '=!' as shell metacharacters / dangerous constructs.
- Fix the misleading "security disabled" startup log.
- Update README and tests.
